name: sim.getObjectChild
description: Retrieves the handle of an object's child object
luaSynopsis: int childHandle = sim.getObjectChild(int objectHandle, int index)
pythonSynopsis: int childHandle = sim.getObjectChild(int objectHandle, int index)
inputs:
1. objectHandle: handle of the object, or sim.handle_scene to retrieve orphan objects
2. index: zero-based index of the child's position. To retrieve all children of an object, call the function by increasing the index until the return value is -1
outputs:
1. childHandle: handle of child object or -1 if the child doesn't exist at that index
replacedBy:
- name: children, class: sceneObject, file: sceneObject_children.property
